    "result_text": "The build is green \u2014 the sole test class passes, including the new `coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` acceptance test.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the daily owner-creation cap, mirroring the existing per-city limit feature so each piece of logic sits where it belongs and reuses established patterns.\n\n**New pieces:**\n- `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (`rest/error/`) \u2014 carries the exhausted registration date, parallel to `CityOwnerLimitExceededException`.\n- `DailyOwnerLimitValidator` (`rest/validation/`) \u2014 a `@Component` with `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100` that rejects when `countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate.now()) >= 100`.\n\n**Wiring through the existing layers:**\n- `OwnerRepository.countByRegistrationDate(LocalDate)` \u2014 declared on the interface and implemented in all three backends (Spring Data JPA `@Query`, JPA `EntityManager` query, and JDBC `SELECT COUNT(*) ... WHERE registration_date=:registrationDate`), matching the `countByCity` idiom.\n- `ClinicService.countOwnersRegisteredOn(LocalDate)` + impl delegating to the repository.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` now calls `dailyOwnerLimitValidator.validate()` alongside the other validators (constructor-injected).\n- `ExceptionControllerAdvice` maps `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` \u2192 **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\nThe count keys off `registrationDate`, which new owners default to the current date via the existing `@PrePersist` hook, so today's registrations are counted correctly.",
